 find out if it's possible to wash off an applied texture so you can restore it to the original one.\n\nFrom this:\n\n<img width=\"1302\" height=\"272\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f3fdff71-7be6-4b2e-a365-6d52cd074c81\" />\n\nTo this:\n\n<img width=\"696\" height=\"232\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eceee793-7a7a-4e5c-986d-4924815a4b12\" />\n\nI did try some things like using the paint kit again to revert it but no clue if it's possible that way, and also tried using a cauldron with water but nope...","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tom5454/Toms-Storage/issues/800/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tom5454/Toms-Storage/issues/800/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tom5454/Toms-Storage/issues/798","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tom5454/Toms-Storage","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tom5454/Toms-Storage/issues/798/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tom5454/Toms-Storage/issues/798/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tom5454/Toms-Storage/issues/798/events","html_url":"https://github.com/tom5454/Toms-Storage/issues/798","id":5594498406,"node_id":"I_kwDOD2xsYc8AAAABTXVFZg","number":798,"title":"[NeoForge 26.2] Inventory Interface crashes dedicated server when external hopper inserts into network and active destination inventory is removed","user":{"login":"ImLith","id":106890578,"node_id":"U_kgDOBl8FUg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106890578?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImLith","html_url":"https://github.com/ImLith","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImLith/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImLith/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImLith/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImLith/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImLith/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImLith/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImLith/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImLith/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ImLith/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-09-26T13:55:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T19:01:15Z","closed_at":"2026-10-15T19:01:15Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Minecraft version: 26.2\nMod version: 2.11.2 (Latest)\nLauncher: NeoForge\n\nDiscovered this while making an auto-smelting furnace.\nOn top of the furnace, I have a basic inventory hopper set to `Raw Iron`.\nOn the back, a basic inventory hopper set to `coal`.\nAt the bottom: a vanilla hopper going into an inventory interface.\nOn the network: a single vanilla chest connected via an inventory cable connector.\n\n<img width=\"913\" height=\"936\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/808b4b72-3eea-4a16-8b1a-f36f9ac964c3\" />\n\nIf you break your chest while it tries to insert the item into the chest, it instantly crashes the entire server.\n\nServer crash report logs: https://pastebin.com/DPb0Y3aG\nWith a single vanilla furnace, it might be hard to replicate. Having more furnaces, or a fast furnace from other mods like `Iron Furnace` can help to reproduce it. But I managed to reproduce the same crash with the exact setup as in the photo.\n\nNOTE\nBreaking the inventory cable connector instead of a chest does NOT crash the server (from my testing).\nHaving an inventory connector instead of an inventory cable connected and breaking the chest still crashes the server.\n\nUsing `Basic Inventory Hopper` to pull stuff out instead of a regular hopper + inventory interface does NOT crash the server (from my testing).\nBut Basic Inventory Hopper is too slow, so an inventory interface is used to speed (since it can accept any speed what it seems). \nSo sounds like an interface issue. `PlatformMultiInventoryAccess` does not safely handle a backing inventory disappearing while an external NeoForge `ResourceHandler` operation is in progress.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tom5454/Toms-Storage/issues/798/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tom5454/Toms-Storage/issues/798/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}